BOOK:Constraints
NUMBER: 1 CONDITION: Point_Constraints
CONDTYPE: over points
CONDMESHTYPE: over nodes
HELP: Use this condition to prescribe the displacement of selected points.\nEvery marked flag will prescribe the movement for that degree of freedom.\nThe values fields permmit to set a prescribed displacementfor that degree.\nUnits in International System for values are:\n\t (m) for the displacements.
TITLE: Flags
QUESTION: Local_Axes#LA#(-GLOBAL-)
VALUE: -GLOBAL-
HELP: If the direction to prescribe is not coincident with the global axes, it is possible to define a set of local axes and prescribe the displacements related to that local axes. To see the defined local axes use button 'Draw'.
QUESTION: X_Constraint#CB#(1,0)
VALUE: 1
DEPENDENCIES: (0,SET,X_Value,0.0)(#DEFAULT#,RESTORE,X_Value,#CURRENT#)
QUESTION: Y_Constraint#CB#(1,0)
VALUE: 1
DEPENDENCIES: (0,SET,Y_Value,0.0)(#DEFAULT#,RESTORE,Y_Value,#CURRENT#)
QUESTION: Z_Constraint#CB#(1,0)
VALUE: 1
DEPENDENCIES: (0,SET,Z_Value,0.0)(#DEFAULT#,RESTORE,Z_Value,#CURRENT#)
TITLE: Values
QUESTION: Units#CB#(N-m-kg,N-cm-kg,N-mm-kg,Kp-cm-utm)
VALUE: N-m-kg
QUESTION: X_Value
VALUE: 0.0
QUESTION: Y_Value
VALUE: 0.0
QUESTION: Z_Value
VALUE: 0.0
END CONDITION
NUMBER: 2 CONDITION: Line_Constraints
CONDTYPE: over lines
CONDMESHTYPE: over nodes
HELP: Use this condition to prescribe the displacement of all the nodes that belong to the line.\nEvery marked flag will prescribe the movement for that degree of freedom.\nThe values fields permmit to set a prescribed displacement for that degree.\nUnits in International System for values are:\n\t (m) for the displacements.
TITLE: Flags
QUESTION: Local_Axes#LA#(-GLOBAL-,-Automatic-)
VALUE: -GLOBAL-
HELP: If the direction to prescribe is not coincident with the global axes, it is possible to define a set of local axes and prescribe the displacements related to that local axes. To see the defined local axes use button 'Draw'.
QUESTION: X_Constraint#CB#(1,0)
VALUE: 1
DEPENDENCIES: (0,SET,X_Value,0.0)(#DEFAULT#,RESTORE,X_Value,#CURRENT#)
QUESTION: Y_Constraint#CB#(1,0)
VALUE: 1
DEPENDENCIES: (0,SET,Y_Value,0.0)(#DEFAULT#,RESTORE,Y_Value,#CURRENT#)
QUESTION: Z_Constraint#CB#(1,0)
VALUE: 1
DEPENDENCIES: (0,SET,Z_Value,0.0)(#DEFAULT#,RESTORE,Z_Value,#CURRENT#)
TITLE: Values
QUESTION: Units#CB#(N-m-kg,N-cm-kg,N-mm-kg,Kp-cm-utm)
VALUE: N-m-kg
QUESTION: X_Value
VALUE: 0.0
QUESTION: Y_Value
VALUE: 0.0
QUESTION: Z_Value
VALUE: 0.0
END CONDITION
NUMBER: 3 CONDITION: Surface_Constraints
CONDTYPE: over surfaces
CONDMESHTYPE: over nodes
HELP: Use this condition to prescribe the displacement of all the nodes that belong to the surface.\nEvery marked flag will prescribe the movement for that degree of freedom.\nThe values fields permmit to set a prescribed displacement for that degree.\nUnits in International System for values are:\n\t (m) for the displacements.
TITLE: Flags
QUESTION: Local_Axes#LA#(-GLOBAL-,-Automatic-)
VALUE: -GLOBAL-
HELP: If the direction to prescribe is not coincident with the global axes, it is possible to define a set of local axes and prescribe the displacements related to that local axes. To see the defined local axes use button 'Draw'.
QUESTION: X_Constraint#CB#(1,0)
VALUE: 1
DEPENDENCIES: (0,SET,X_Value,0.0)(#DEFAULT#,RESTORE,X_Value,#CURRENT#)
QUESTION: Y_Constraint#CB#(1,0)
VALUE: 1
DEPENDENCIES: (0,SET,Y_Value,0.0)(#DEFAULT#,RESTORE,Y_Value,#CURRENT#)
QUESTION: Z_Constraint#CB#(1,0)
VALUE: 1
DEPENDENCIES: (0,SET,Z_Value,0.0)(#DEFAULT#,RESTORE,Z_Value,#CURRENT#)
TITLE: Values
QUESTION: Units#CB#(N-m-kg,N-cm-kg,N-mm-kg,Kp-cm-utm)
VALUE: N-m-kg
QUESTION: X_Value
VALUE: 0.0
QUESTION: Y_Value
VALUE: 0.0
QUESTION: Z_Value
VALUE: 0.0
END CONDITION
NUMBER: 4 CONDITION: Surface_Elastic_Constraints
CONDTYPE: over surfaces
CONDMESHTYPE: over face elements
HELP: Use this condition to apply an elastic spring to the displacement of all nodes that belong to the surface.\nEvery marked flag will prescribe the spring for that degree of freedom.\nEnter the stiffness constant for every actived degree of freedom in the values fields.\nUnits in International System for stiffness constants are:\n\t (N/m3) for the displacements.
TITLE: Flags
QUESTION: Local_Axes#LA#(-GLOBAL-,-Automatic-)
VALUE: -GLOBAL-
HELP: If the direction to prescribe is not coincident with the global axes, it is possible to define a set of local axes and prescribe the displacements related to that local axes. To see the defined local axes use button 'Draw'.
QUESTION: X_Constraint#CB#(1,0)
VALUE: 1
DEPENDENCIES: (0,SET,X_Value,0.0)(#DEFAULT#,RESTORE,X_Value,#CURRENT#)
QUESTION: Y_Constraint#CB#(1,0)
VALUE: 1
DEPENDENCIES: (0,SET,Y_Value,0.0)(#DEFAULT#,RESTORE,Y_Value,#CURRENT#)
QUESTION: Z_Constraint#CB#(1,0)
VALUE: 1
DEPENDENCIES: (0,SET,Z_Value,0.0)(#DEFAULT#,RESTORE,Z_Value,#CURRENT#)
TITLE: Values
QUESTION: Units#CB#(N-m-kg,N-cm-kg,N-mm-kg,Kp-cm-utm)
VALUE: N-m-kg
QUESTION: X_Value
VALUE: 0.0
QUESTION: Y_Value
VALUE: 0.0
QUESTION: Z_Value
VALUE: 0.0
END CONDITION
BOOK:Static Loads
NUMBER: 5 CONDITION: Punctual_Load
CONDTYPE: over points
CONDMESHTYPE: over nodes
HELP: A force applied to the selected points of the model. Units in International System for values are:\n\t (N) for the forces.
QUESTION: Units#CB#(N-m-kg,N-cm-kg,N-mm-kg,Kp-cm-utm)
VALUE: N-m-kg
QUESTION: X_Force
VALUE: 0.0
QUESTION: Y_Force
VALUE: 0.0
QUESTION: Z_Force
VALUE: 0.0
END CONDITION
NUMBER: 6 CONDITION: Self_weight_solid
CONDTYPE: over volumes
CONDMESHTYPE: over body elements
HELP: If this condition is applied to solids, a load is calculated and assigned, depending on the self-weight of the material, the volume of the solid and the direction of the gravity.
QUESTION: Self_weight_load#CB#(.)
VALUE: -
END CONDITION
NUMBER: 7 CONDITION: Global_Pressure_Load
CONDTYPE: over surfaces
CONDMESHTYPE: over face elements
HELP: A pressure load over the contour of the solid given in global axes. Units in International System for values are:\n\t (N/m2) for the pressures.
QUESTION: Units#CB#(N-m-kg,N-cm-kg,N-mm-kg,Kp-cm-utm)
VALUE: N-m-kg
QUESTION: X_Pressure
VALUE: 0.0
QUESTION: Y_Pressure
VALUE: 0.0
QUESTION: Z_Pressure
VALUE: 0.0
END CONDITION
NUMBER: 8 CONDITION: Global_Projected_Pressure_Load
CONDTYPE: over surfaces
CONDMESHTYPE: over face elements
HELP: A pressure load over the contour of the solid given in global axes and projected as if the area of the contour was the projected area over the pressure vector. Units in International System for values are:\n\t (N/m2) for the pressures.
QUESTION: Units#CB#(N-m-kg,N-cm-kg,N-mm-kg,Kp-cm-utm)
VALUE: N-m-kg
QUESTION: X_Pressure
VALUE: 0.0
QUESTION: Y_Pressure
VALUE: 0.0
QUESTION: Z_Pressure
VALUE: 0.0
END CONDITION
NUMBER: 9 CONDITION: Local_Pressure_Load
CONDTYPE: over surfaces
CONDMESHTYPE: over face elements
HELP: A pressure load over the contour of the solid orthogonal to this contour. Positive pressures point indwards the solid. Units in International System for values are:\n\t (N/m2) for the pressures.
QUESTION: Units#CB#(N-m-kg,N-cm-kg,N-mm-kg,Kp-cm-utm)
VALUE: N-m-kg
QUESTION: Normal_inwards
VALUE: 0.0
END CONDITION
NUMBER: 10 CONDITION: Solid_triangular_Load
CONDTYPE: over surfaces
CONDMESHTYPE: over face elements
HELP: This load is similar to that of 'Global_Pressure__Load' but its intensity changes depending on the point where it is applied. The two points define an imaginary line in the space. For every point of the volume contour  where the load is applied, it is possible to project this point on the imaginary line and interpolate the values related to these points depending on where it is projected. \nUnits in International System for values are:\n\t (m) for the points\n\t(N/m2) for the pressures.
TITLE: Position
QUESTION: Units#CB#(N-m-kg,N-cm-kg,N-mm-kg,Kp-cm-utm)
VALUE: N-m-kg
QUESTION: X_point_1
VALUE: 0.0
QUESTION: Y_point_1
VALUE: 0.0
QUESTION: Z_point_1
VALUE: 0.0
QUESTION: X_point_2
VALUE: 0.0
QUESTION: Y_point_2
VALUE: 0.0
QUESTION: Z_point_2
VALUE: 0.0
TITLE: Pressures
QUESTION: Local_Axes#LA#(-GLOBAL-,-Automatic-)
VALUE: -GLOBAL-
QUESTION: X_pressure_1
VALUE: 0.0
QUESTION: Y_pressure_1
VALUE: 0.0
QUESTION: Z_pressure_1
VALUE: 0.0
QUESTION: X_pressure_2
VALUE: 0.0
QUESTION: Y_pressure_2
VALUE: 0.0
QUESTION: Z_pressure_2
VALUE: 0.0
END CONDITION
NUMBER: 11 CONDITION: Solid_hydrostatic_Load
CONDTYPE: over surfaces
CONDMESHTYPE: over face elements
HELP: This is a triangular load that has value 0.0 at the reference coordinate (in the sense of the gravity) and gives an hydrostatic pressure that depends on the self-weight of the water or terrain. \nUnits in International System for values are:\n\t (m) for the coordinates\n\t(N/m3) for the self-weight.
QUESTION: Units#CB#(N-m-kg,N-cm-kg,N-mm-kg,Kp-cm-utm)
VALUE: N-m-kg
QUESTION: Reference_coordinate:
VALUE: 0.0
QUESTION: Self_weight_water:
VALUE: 10000
END CONDITION
NUMBER: 12 CONDITION: Temperature
CONDTYPE: over volumes
CONDMESHTYPE: over body elements
HELP: This condition considers the deformation supported by the solid when there is a uniform temperature change in all the solid.
QUESTION: \u03B1 (1/\u00B0C)
VALUE: 0.000012
QUESTION: \u0394T (\u00B0C)
VALUE: 0.0
END CONDITION
NUMBER: 13 CONDITION: Tdyn_Strain
CONDTYPE: over volumes
CONDMESHTYPE: over body elements
HELP: This condition considers the deformation supported by the solid when there is a change of temperature in all the solid imported from the thermal module Tdyn.
QUESTION: Noop
VALUE: -
STATE: HIDDEN
END CONDITION
BOOK:Properties
NUMBER: 14 CONDITION: Solid
CONDTYPE: over volumes
CONDMESHTYPE: over body elements
HELP: This property must be assigned to volumes. 'E' is the Young Modulus and 'nu' is the Poisson coefficient. \nUnits in International System for values are:\n\t(N/m2) for 'E'\n\t(adimensional) nu\n\t(N/m3) for the Specific_weight.
QUESTION: Units#CB#(N-m-kg,N-cm-kg,N-mm-kg,Kp-cm-utm)
VALUE: N-m-kg
QUESTION: E
VALUE: 2.1e11
QUESTION: nu
VALUE: 0.3
QUESTION: Specific_weight
VALUE: 0.0
END CONDITION
BOOK:Special properties
NUMBER: 15 CONDITION: Non_analysis_triangles
CONDTYPE: over surfaces
CONDMESHTYPE: over body elements
HELP: This property must be assigned to triangles that will not be read but are only for decoration.TEXT: Decorative elements
QUESTION: Noop
VALUE: -
STATE: HIDDEN
END CONDITION
BOOK:Detailed results
NUMBER: 16 CONDITION: Detailed_results
CONDTYPE: over points
CONDMESHTYPE: over nodes
HELP: If this condition is applied to points, an additional file is created: PROJECT.detailed.xml with detailed result information in the selected nodes.
QUESTION: Id
VALUE: pointA
END CONDITION
BOOK:Dynamic Loads
NUMBER: 17 CONDITION: Dynamic-Point_Load
